{
  "id": "Lyo.Trakt.Client",
  "name": "Lyo.Trakt.Client",
  "area": "Integration",
  "tagline": "Typed HTTP client for the Trakt catalog and OAuth APIs.",
  "description": "Typed HTTP client for [Trakt](https://trakt.tv/) catalog search and OAuth.\n\n**Archetype C (vendor client).** Catalog calls use `https://api.trakt.tv` with `trakt-api-version: 2` and `trakt-api-key`. OAuth calls use `https://auth.trakt.tv`. The client returns access and refresh tokens and does not store a user bearer. Refresh tokens are single-use.\n\nDevice-token polling returns pending, expired, denied, and slow-down as `TraktDevicePoll.Status`. List calls return `TraktPage<T>` from the `X-Pagination-*` headers. Trending and search rows are wrappers. `GET /shows/{id}/seasons/{season}` returns episodes. Show status stays the API string, including `returning series`.",
  "features": [
    "**Search.** `GET /search/movie` and `GET /search/{idType}/{id}`. IMDb lookup keeps the `tt` prefix.",
    "**Movies.** `GET /movies/{id}` and `GET /movies/trending` (`watchers` plus `movie`).",
    "**Seasons.** `GET /shows/{id}/seasons/{season}` returns an episode array.",
    "**OAuth.** Authorization-code exchange and device-token polling on `https://auth.trakt.tv`."
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "title": "Register",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "services.AddTraktClientFromConfiguration(builder.Configuration);\n\nservices.AddTraktClient(o => {\n    o.ClientId = \"your-client-id\";\n    o.ClientSecret = \"your-client-secret\";\n    o.RedirectUri = \"https://app.example/callback\";\n});"
    },
    {
      "title": "Search and exchange a code",
      "language": "csharp",
      "code": "var page = await client.Search.SearchMoviesAsync(\"weapons\", ct);\nvar movie = page.Items[0].Movie;\nvar token = await client.Auth.ExchangeCodeAsync(code, ct);\n// Store token.RefreshToken. The next refresh must send that value."
    }
  ],
